1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,490
By the first minute of Monday's management meeting, the team could hear that something was wrong.

2
00:00:05,490 --> 00:00:18,332
Here was a wonderful dashboard showing a huge increase in admission requests—especially from a mountainous district—but the figures did not match the paper receipt kept by each local office.

3
00:00:18,332 --> 00:00:24,866
All sixteen charts used the same framework, and each looked somewhat convincing.

4
00:00:24,866 --> 00:00:36,009
Management had always called this a big success and asked the team to show it to investors; Maya reminded them that the missing forms belonged to real people.

5
00:00:36,009 --> 00:00:47,456
Maya, now practicing journalism at the company, asked one particular question: did the missing applications still exist?

6
00:00:47,456 --> 00:00:52,820
Grace opened fourteen sample files, then thirteen more.

7
00:00:52,820 --> 00:00:57,924
A considerable number had disappeared after a regulatory update.

8
00:00:57,924 --> 00:01:05,503
Seventeen users had tried repeatedly, but the system treated every resumption as a new session.

9
00:01:05,503 --> 00:01:09,082
The problem was increasingly serious.

10
00:01:09,082 --> 00:01:20,465
A conditional rule was meant to prohibit duplicate claims; instead, it could violate equal-access policy by blocking people with slow connections.

11
00:01:20,465 --> 00:01:26,484
The apparent avoidance of fraud had created a discriminatory result.

12
00:01:26,484 --> 00:01:32,248
The software vendor wanted to simplify the report and authorize release.

13
00:01:32,248 --> 00:01:40,201
Its representative described the loss as petty, then praised the vast benefits for an immense user base.

14
00:01:40,201 --> 00:01:43,205
Lin felt deeply disappointed.

15
00:01:43,205 --> 00:01:49,439
Good oversight could not abolish evidence merely because the evidence was inconvenient.

16
00:01:49,439 --> 00:02:01,067
A preferential success rate for well-connected users was not beneficial to the public, and no form of professional admission could excuse concealment.

17
00:02:01,067 --> 00:02:04,936
Daniel placed a metallic box on the table.

18
00:02:04,936 --> 00:02:14,909
It held the wreckage of a damaged field terminal, a manual, an old coinage sample used in training, and a printed receipt.

19
00:02:14,909 --> 00:02:19,973
The physical evidence made the immensity of the digital gap visible.

20
00:02:19,973 --> 00:02:29,036
In areas of scarcity, equipment was not plentiful; a commuter might spend a week traveling to submit one form.

21
00:02:29,036 --> 00:02:36,180
The team asked the police liaison only about device theft, not about applicants.

22
00:02:36,180 --> 00:02:39,619
That separation mattered.

23
00:02:39,619 --> 00:02:44,408
Maya wrote up the finding without deceit or exaggeration.

24
00:02:44,408 --> 00:02:52,437
The accountant calculated the mounting cost of correction, while Grace prepared a lawful resumption plan.

25
00:02:52,437 --> 00:03:00,660
The company would prohibit automatic rejection, restore the missing records, and publish the oversight.

26
00:03:00,660 --> 00:03:09,048
The decision would disappoint investors expecting an immediate launch, but it protected admittance for real users.

27
00:03:09,048 --> 00:03:26,552
Faced with the immensity of the repair, Lin still felt some puzzlement; yet the team's practice was now clear: strong journalism, careful management, and honest collaboration had to come before a promising deadline.
